-- Liberty HomeCare (UW-RPP-W-001-06-V): the General Conditions (CÁC ĐIỀU KIỆN CHUNG), 1-14,
-- and the Deductible definition they apply. Quotations (`src:N`) are line N of
-- ../../source/raw/liberty-homecare.txt.
--
-- THREE KINDS OF RULE HERE, kept apart:
-- * grounds on which a claim fails (GC1, GC2, GC3, GC4 through GC1, GC5, GC7, GC12): a list,
--   like the exclusions, so an answer names the clause;
-- * amounts (GC9 contribution, GC11 refunds and the short-period scale, GC13 Deductible);
-- * duties and powers with their deadlines (GC4, GC5, GC6, GC8, GC10, GC11, GC12), as
--   regulative rules. THE UNIT OF EVERY `WITHIN` IN THIS FILE IS ONE CALENDAR DAY, and a
--   trace starts AT 0 on the day of the event the duty runs from. The document does not say
--   whether its "days" are calendar or working days (fork F-days: calendar, taken).
--
-- src:800 | CÁC ĐIỀU KIỆN CHUNG

§ `General Conditions`

DECLARE `A Part` IS ONE OF
    `Part 1`
    `Part 2`
    `Part 3`

DECLARE `A ground under the General Conditions` IS ONE OF
    `GC1: the terms of the policy were not observed`
    `GC1: a statement in the Proposal Form was untrue`
    `GC2: the Insurer avoided the policy for misdescription`
    `GC3(a): the Insured Location used other than as a residence`
    `GC3(b): precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk`
    `GC3(c): the property moved to another building or place`
    `GC3(d): the Home vacant for more than 30 days`
    `GC3(e): the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law`
    `GC1 with GC4(a): no immediate written notice with full particulars`
    `GC1 with GC4(b): a writ, summons or notice not forwarded on receipt`
    `GC1 with GC4(c): liability admitted or payment offered without written consent`
    `GC1 with GC4(d): the police not notified of a theft or malicious act`
    `GC1 with GC4(e): no immediate action to minimise the loss`
    `GC1 with GC4(f): other insurances not disclosed`
    `GC1 with GC4(g): no written claim within 30 days or the time allowed`
    `GC1 with Part 1: no receipts or proof of value kept`
    `GC1 with GC12: reasonable precautions not taken`
    `GC5: the Insured obstructed the Insurer or did not comply with its requirements`
    `GC7(a): the claim is fraudulent`
    `GC7(a): fraudulent means or devices were used`
    `GC7(a): the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance`
    `GC7(b)(i): rejected, and not challenged within 12 months`
    `GC7(b)(ii): decided by arbitration, and not challenged within 12 months`

§§ `GC1. Due observance`

-- Due observance and fulfilment of the terms, conditions, exclusions, limits and endorsements
-- so far as they relate to anything the Insured must do or comply with, and the truth of the
-- statements and answers in the Proposal Form, are conditions precedent to any liability of
-- the Insurer to make any payment.
