-- Input convention: the facts in `The Insured's conduct` describe changes that affect what is
-- claimed for. "More than 30 days" is strict: 30 days vacant is not a GC3(d) change.

§§ `GC4. Claims procedure`

-- On any Insured Event that may give rise to a claim the Insured shall: (a) immediately give
-- written notice with full particulars; (b) forward every writ, summons, court order or other
-- notice on receipt; (c) not admit liability or offer or promise payment without written
-- consent; (d) for theft or malicious persons, immediately notify the police and assist; (e)
-- act immediately to minimise the loss and prevent more; (f) disclose all other insurances;
-- (g) deliver a written claim with particulars and evidence (and if required a statutory
-- declaration) within 30 days of the event or any longer time the Insurer allows in writing,
-- at the Insured's expense.
