-- F-gc4g: the 30 days run from the day of the event, which is day 0; a claim delivered on
-- day 30 is in time; the Insurer's written extension is recorded as the last day it allows.
-- LAW: art 30(1) (aid, lines 706-710) fixes the time for submitting a claim at one year from
-- the insured event, and art 30(3) runs it from the third party's demand for a liability
-- claim. GC4(g)'s 30 days is shorter; the conflict is recorded (finding X-claim-time), not resolved here.
@ref GC4(g), src:848-852 (fork F-gc4g)
GIVEN `the date of the event`        IS A DATE
      `the date allowed in writing`  IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`GC4(g): the last day for the written claim on an event of` `the date of the event` `, extended to` `the date allowed in writing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date allowed in writing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `day 30`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN IF d AT LEAST `day 30` THEN d ELSE `day 30`
    WHERE
        `day 30` MEANS `the date of the event` PLUS 30

§§ `GC5. The Insurer's rights after a loss`

-- On loss of or damage to insured property the Insurer may (a) enter and take possession of
-- the building or premises; (b) take possession of or require delivery of any property of the
-- Insured there; (c) keep possession and examine, sort, arrange, remove or otherwise deal with
-- it; (d) sell it or dispose of it. These powers last until the Insured gives written notice
-- that no claim is made, or the claim is finally settled or withdrawn, and their exercise
-- creates no liability and waives no right.
