§§ `GC6. Reinstatement`

-- The Insurer may at its option reinstate or replace instead of paying, alone or with other
-- insurers; it is not bound to reinstate exactly but only as circumstances permit and in a
-- reasonably sufficient manner, and never to spend more than it would have cost to reinstate
-- at the time of the loss, nor more than the sum insured on the property.
