-- src:941 | nhưng không giới hạn bởi, tranh chấp về số tiền bồi thường theo Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm, thì bất kỳ
-- src:942 | bên nào cũng có quyền đệ trình tranh chấp đó đến Trung tâm Trọng tài Quốc tế Việt Nam (VIAC)
-- src:943 | để được giải quyết theo các quy tắc tố tụng trọng tài có hiệu lực tại thời điểm tranh chấp. Hội đồng
-- src:944 | trọng tài sẽ gồm một (1) thành viên và việc xét xử bằng trọng tài sẽ được thực hiện tại Thành phố
-- src:945 | Hồ Chí Minh và bằng tiếng Việt. Phán quyết của trọng tài sẽ có giá trị chung thẩm và ràng buộc về
-- src:946 | mặt pháp lý đối với cả hai bên.
@ref GC10, src:939-946
GIVETH A STRING
`GC10: the forum, if either party chooses arbitration` MEANS
    "VIAC; one arbitrator; seat Ho Chi Minh City; Vietnamese; the award final and binding"

§§ `GC11. Cancellation`

-- The Insurer may cancel by 30 days' written notice by registered post to the Insured's last
-- registered address, refunding the premium paid less the pro rata premium for the time the
-- policy has been in force.
-- src:947 | 11. Hủy bỏ Hợp đồng
-- src:948 | Công Ty Bảo Hiểm có thể hủy bỏ Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm bằng cách gửi một văn bản thông báo bằng
-- src:949 | thư đảm bảo cho Người Được Bảo Hiểm trước 30 ngày tới địa chỉ đăng ký cuối cùng của Người
-- src:950 | Được Bảo Hiểm, trong trường hợp đó Công Ty Bảo Hiểm sẽ hoàn trả cho Người Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:951 | khoản phí bảo hiểm đã thanh toán sau khi trừ đi khoản phí bảo hiểm tính theo tỷ lệ thời gian tương
-- src:952 | ứng với Thời Hạn Bảo Hiểm đã có hiệu lực.
-- The Insured may cancel at any time by written notice, and is refunded the premium less the
-- premium for the time in force at the Insurer's short-period scale.
-- src:953 | Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm cũng có thể được hủy bỏ bởi Người Được Bảo Hiểm tại bất kỳ thời điểm nào
-- src:954 | bằng cách gửi một văn bản thông báo cho Công Ty Bảo Hiểm, trong trường hợp đó Người Được
-- src:955 | Bảo Hiểm sẽ được hoàn lại một khoản phí sau khi trừ đi khoản phí cho thời gian Hợp đồng Bảo
-- src:956 | hiểm có hiệu lực tính theo biểu phí ngắn hạn sau đây của Công Ty Bảo Hiểm:
-- F-gc11-notice: the 30 days run from the day the notice is sent (the document says "send
-- ... 30 days before"); receipt is not mentioned. LAW: art 26 (aid, lines 623-635) lists the
-- cases in which either party may terminate unilaterally; GC11 lets either party cancel
-- without a cause. Noted, not encoded.
@ref GC11, src:947-952 (fork F-gc11-notice)
GIVEN `the date the notice is sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`GC11: the day an Insurer's cancellation takes effect, the notice sent on` `the date the notice is sent` MEANS
    `the date the notice is sent` PLUS 30

-- The short-period scale, one L4 row per printed row. "Đến 3 tháng" is "up to 3 months";
-- "Từ 3 tháng đến 6 tháng" is "from 3 to 6 months"; so 3 months and 6 months fall in two
-- rows each. F-short-period: the rows are read in printed order and the first that fits
-- wins, so exactly 3 months is 30% and exactly 6 months is 60% (the reading Law art 24, aid
-- lines 588-591, would favour). "Trên 9 tháng" is strictly over 9 months.
-- src:957 | Biểu Phí Ngắn Hạn
-- src:958 | Thời hạn Phí Bảo Hiểm
-- src:959 | Đến 3 tháng 30% trên Phí Bảo hiểm năm
-- src:960 | Từ 3 tháng đến 6 tháng 60% trên Phí Bảo hiểm năm
-- src:961 | Từ 6 tháng đến 9 tháng 90% trên Phí Bảo hiểm năm
-- src:962 | Trên 9 tháng 100% trên Phí Bảo hiểm năm
DECLARE `A row of the short-period scale` HAS
    `in force for at most this many months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the share of the annual premium`       IS A NUMBER

@ref GC11, Biểu Phí Ngắn Hạn, src:957-962 (fork F-short-period)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A row of the short-period scale`
`the short-period scale` MEANS
    --                                     at most N months, share
    LIST (`A row of the short-period scale` OF JUST 3,  30%)   -- src:959 Đến 3 tháng
       , (`A row of the short-period scale` OF JUST 6,  60%)   -- src:960 Từ 3 tháng đến 6 tháng
       , (`A row of the short-period scale` OF JUST 9,  90%)   -- src:961 Từ 6 tháng đến 9 tháng
       , (`A row of the short-period scale` OF NOTHING, 100%)  -- src:962 Trên 9 tháng

-- "In force for at most N months": the cancellation takes effect no later than N calendar
-- months after the Period began.
@ref GC11, src:953-962
GIVEN summary   IS A `The Policy Summary`
      `ends on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GC11: the short-period share for a policy under` summary `cancelled by the Insured with effect on` `ends on` MEANS
    `the first row that fits` `the short-period scale`
    WHERE
        `fits` row MEANS
            CONSIDER row's `in force for at most this many months`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST m  THEN `ends on` AT MOST `add months` (summary's `the Period of Insurance begins`) m
        `the first row that fits` rows MEANS
            CONSIDER rows
            WHEN EMPTY THEN 1
            WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN IF `fits` r THEN r's `the share of the annual premium` ELSE `the first row that fits` rest

-- The refund on the Insured's cancellation. F-gc11-refund: never negative; GC11 gives the
-- Insurer no claim for more premium.
@ref GC11, src:953-956 (fork F-gc11-refund)
GIVEN policy  IS A `The policy`
      `ends on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GC11: the refund to an Insured who cancels, under` policy `with effect on` `ends on` MEANS
    max 0 (policy's `the premium paid` MINUS `the short-period premium`)
    WHERE
        `the short-period premium` MEANS
            policy's `the Policy Summary`'s `the annual premium`
                TIMES `GC11: the short-period share for a policy under` (policy's `the Policy Summary`) `cancelled by the Insured with effect on` `ends on`

-- The refund on the Insurer's cancellation: the premium paid less the pro rata premium for
-- the time in force. F-gc11-pro-rata: days in force are counted from the first day of the
-- Period to the day cancellation takes effect; the Period has (last day - first day + 1) days.
@ref GC11, src:947-952 (fork F-gc11-pro-rata)
GIVEN policy  IS A `The policy`
      `ends on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GC11: the refund when the Insurer cancels, under` policy `with effect on` `ends on` MEANS
    max 0 (policy's `the premium paid` MINUS policy's `the premium paid` TIMES `days in force` DIVIDED BY `days in the Period`)
    WHERE
        `begins`             MEANS policy's `the Policy Summary`'s `the Period of Insurance begins`
        `days in force`      MEANS min (Day `ends on` MINUS Day `begins`) `days in the Period`
        `days in the Period` MEANS Day (policy's `the Policy Summary`'s `the Period of Insurance ends`) MINUS Day `begins` PLUS 1

§§ `GC12. Reasonable precautions`

-- At the Insured's expense, reasonable precautions to prevent loss, liability, accident or
-- injury, including (a) maintaining property in proper repair; (b) securing doors, windows
-- and other openings; (c) complying with statutory requirements; (d) complying with
-- manufacturers' recommendations; (e) all reasonable recommendations of the Insurer. Limb (e)
-- gives the Insurer an open power to add requirements (finding X-discretion).
-- src:963 | 12. Các Biện pháp Đề phòng Hợp lý
-- src:964 | Bằng chi phí của mình, Người Được Bảo Hiểm phải thực hiện các biện pháp đề phòng hợp lý để
-- src:965 | ngăn ngừa tổn thất hoặc thiệt hại, các tổn thất liên quan đến trách nhiệm, tai nạn hoặc thương tật,
-- src:966 | bao gồm:
-- src:967 | (a) việc bảo dưỡng tài sản trong tình trạng được sửa chữa đúng đắn;
-- src:968 | (b) bảo đảm an toàn các cửa đi và cửa sổ và các lối vào khác;
-- src:969 | (c) tuân thủ các yêu cầu theo luật định;
-- src:970 | (d) tuân thủ các đề nghị của nhà sản xuất;
-- src:971 | (e) tất cả các đề nghị hợp lý của Công Ty Bảo Hiểm.

§§ `GC13. Deductible`

-- The Deductible is the part of a claim the Insured bears:
-- src:284 | Mức Miễn Thường
-- src:285 | Một phần của số tiền bồi thường mà Người Được Bảo Hiểm phải chịu.
-- The Insurer is not liable for the Deductible stated in the Policy Summary. It applies to
-- each and every loss at each separate Insured Location, after all the other terms and
-- conditions have been applied. Where one loss gives rise to claims under several Parts, only
-- the highest Deductible applies.
-- src:972 | 13. Mức Miễn Thường
-- src:973 | Công Ty Bảo Hiểm không có trách nhiệm bồi thường đối với Mức Miễn Thường ghi trong Bản Tóm
-- src:974 | Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm. Mức Miễn Thường được áp dụng với mỗi và mọi tổn thất tại mỗi Địa Điểm
-- src:975 | Bảo Hiểm riêng biệt, sau khi áp dụng tất cả các điều khoản và điều kiện khác của Hợp Đồng Bảo
-- src:976 | Hiểm.
-- src:977 | Nếu có bất kỳ tổn thất hoặc thiệt hại nào dẫn đến yêu cầu bồi thường cho nhiều Phần của Hợp
-- src:978 | Đồng Bảo Hiểm, chỉ có một Mức Miễn Thường cao nhất được áp dụng.
-- F-deductible: a Part for which the Summary states no Deductible has none.
@ref GC13, src:972-978 (fork F-deductible)
GIVEN summary IS A `The Policy Summary`
      part    IS A `A Part`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GC13: the Deductible stated in` summary `for` part MEANS
    fromMaybe 0 (CONSIDER part
                 WHEN `Part 1` THEN summary's `the Part 1 Deductible`
                 WHEN `Part 2` THEN summary's `the Part 2 Deductible`
                 WHEN `Part 3` THEN summary's `the Part 3 Deductible`)

@ref GC13, src:977-978
GIVEN summary IS A `The Policy Summary`
      parts   IS A LIST OF `A Part`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GC13: the one Deductible for a loss under` summary `claimed under` parts MEANS
    foldr max 0 (map (GIVEN p YIELD `GC13: the Deductible stated in` summary `for` p) parts)

-- "After all the other terms and conditions": the Deductible comes off last, and never
-- takes the payment below nothing.
@ref GC13, src:974-976
GIVEN `the Deductible`                    IS A NUMBER
      `the amount after every other term` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`GC13: less the Deductible` `the Deductible` `, payable on` `the amount after every other term` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount after every other term` MINUS `the Deductible`)

§§ `GC14. Law`

-- src:979 | 14. Luật và Tập quán
-- src:980 | Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm sẽ được điều chỉnh và giải thích theo các quy định của pháp luật Việt Nam.
@ref GC14, src:979-980
GIVETH A STRING
`GC14: the governing law` MEANS "the law of Vietnam"

§ `The grounds under the General Conditions`

-- Every ground on which the General Conditions defeat a claim, in source order.
-- `theft or malicious persons` decides whether GC4(d) applies; `the Parts claimed under`
-- decides whether Part 1's proof-of-value duty applies; `as at` is the date the question is
-- asked, for the 30-day and 12-month periods.
@ref General Conditions 1-7 and 12, src:800-915, 963-971; Part 1 proof of value, src:338-341
GIVEN conduct                     IS A `The Insured's conduct`
      `the date of the event`     IS A DATE
      `theft or malicious persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Parts claimed under`   IS A LIST OF `A Part`
      `as at`                     IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under the General Conditions`
`the grounds under the General Conditions on` conduct `, event on` `the date of the event` `, theft` `theft or malicious persons` `, under` `the Parts claimed under` `, as at` `as at` MEANS
    `those that hold among`
        (LIST PAIR `GC1: the terms of the policy were not observed`       (NOT conduct's `observed and fulfilled the terms of the policy`)
            , PAIR `GC1: a statement in the Proposal Form was untrue`     (NOT conduct's `the statements in the Proposal Form were true`)
            , PAIR `GC2: the Insurer avoided the policy for misdescription`
                   (    conduct's `misrepresented, misdescribed or omitted a matter in a document`
                    AND conduct's `the Insurer elected to avoid the policy for misdescription`)
            , PAIR `GC3(a): the Insured Location used other than as a residence` (`unendorsed` (conduct's `the Insured Location was used other than as a residence`))
            , PAIR `GC3(b): precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk` (`unendorsed` (conduct's `precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk`))
            , PAIR `GC3(c): the property moved to another building or place` (`unendorsed` (conduct's `the property was moved to another building or place`))
            , PAIR `GC3(d): the Home vacant for more than 30 days` (`unendorsed` (conduct's `consecutive days the Home had been vacant` GREATER THAN 30))
            , PAIR `GC3(e): the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law` (`unendorsed` (conduct's `the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law`))
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(a): no immediate written notice with full particulars` (NOT conduct's `gave immediate written notice with full particulars`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(b): a writ, summons or notice not forwarded on receipt` (NOT conduct's `forwarded every writ, summons and notice on receipt`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(c): liability admitted or payment offered without written consent` (conduct's `admitted or offered payment without written consent`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(d): the police not notified of a theft or malicious act`
                   (`theft or malicious persons` AND NOT conduct's `notified the police immediately`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(e): no immediate action to minimise the loss` (NOT conduct's `acted immediately to minimise the loss`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(f): other insurances not disclosed` (NOT conduct's `disclosed all other insurances`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC4(g): no written claim within 30 days or the time allowed` `the claim was late`
            , PAIR `GC1 with Part 1: no receipts or proof of value kept`
                   (elem `Part 1` `the Parts claimed under` AND NOT conduct's `kept receipts or proof of value`)
            , PAIR `GC1 with GC12: reasonable precautions not taken` (NOT conduct's `took reasonable precautions`)
            , PAIR `GC5: the Insured obstructed the Insurer or did not comply with its requirements` (conduct's `obstructed or failed to comply with the Insurer's requirements`)
            , PAIR `GC7(a): the claim is fraudulent` (conduct's `the claim is fraudulent in any respect`)
            , PAIR `GC7(a): fraudulent means or devices were used` (conduct's `used fraudulent means or devices`)
            , PAIR `GC7(a): the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance` (conduct's `the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance`)
            , PAIR `GC7(b)(i): rejected, and not challenged within 12 months`
                   (`GC7(b): forfeited, decided on` (conduct's `the date the claim was rejected`) `, challenged on` (conduct's `the date the rejection was challenged`) `, as at` `as at`)
            , PAIR `GC7(b)(ii): decided by arbitration, and not challenged within 12 months`
                   (`GC7(b): forfeited, decided on` (conduct's `the date of an arbitral award on the claim`) `, challenged on` (conduct's `the date the award was challenged`) `, as at` `as at`))
    WHERE
        `unendorsed` change MEANS change AND NOT conduct's `the Insurer endorsed its consent before the loss`
        `the last day` MEANS `GC4(g): the last day for the written claim on an event of` `the date of the event` `, extended to` (conduct's `the date to which the Insurer extended time in writing`)
        `the claim was late` MEANS
            CONSIDER conduct's `the date the written claim was delivered`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `as at` GREATER THAN `the last day`
            WHEN JUST d  THEN d GREATER THAN `the last day`

§ `Duties and powers, with their deadlines`

-- Duties and powers are exercised with #TRACE (a DEONTIC cannot be compared with EQUALS).
-- The clock is in calendar days and AT 0 is the day of the event (see the module header).

§§ `GC4: the Insured's duties after an Insured Event`

-- The notice in (a) is due "immediately" (ngay): no number of days is stated, so it carries no
-- WITHIN and stands until it is given. The written claim in (g) is due within the days
-- allowed (30, or longer if the Insurer allows in writing), counted from the event; both run
-- from the event at once (RAND). When the claim is in, the Insurer must pay: the document
-- states no time for payment (Comparables, "insurer's payment deadline: not stated"). LAW:
-- art 31(1) (aid, lines 718-724) supplies 15 days from receipt of a complete and valid claim
-- file where the contract states none. Noted, not encoded.
@ref GC4(a), (g), src:832-852
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC4: the Insured's notice and claim, with days allowed` `the days allowed` MEANS
        (PARTY  `the Insured`
         MUST   `give written notice of the event with full particulars`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC4(a): no written notice with full particulars of the event")
    RAND
        (PARTY  `the Insured`
         MUST   `deliver a written claim with particulars and evidence`
         WITHIN `the days allowed`
         HENCE  (PARTY `the Insurer`
                 MUST  `pay the claim`
                 HENCE FULFILLED
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the Insurer` BECAUSE "the Insurer did not pay an admitted claim")
         LEST   BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC4(g): no written claim within 30 days of the event or the longer time allowed in writing")

-- GC4(c), and Part 2 Condition 2: the Insured shall not admit, negotiate, offer, promise or
-- pay without the Insurer's written consent. No period is stated, so no WITHIN (a WITHIN
-- would make the prohibition lapse).
@ref GC4(c), src:839-840; Part 2 Condition 2, src:613-615
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC4(c): no admission or offer without written consent` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    SHANT `admit, negotiate, offer, promise or pay without written consent`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC4(c): liability admitted, or payment offered or promised, without the Insurer's written consent"

§§ `GC5: the Insurer's powers, and the Insured's duty not to obstruct`

@ref GC5, src:853-882
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC5: the Insurer may take possession; the Insured shall not obstruct or abandon` MEANS
        (PARTY `the Insurer`
         MAY   `enter and take possession of the premises or property`)
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Insured`
         SHANT `obstruct the Insurer in exercising its powers`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC5: the Insured obstructed the Insurer; all benefit under the policy is forfeited")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Insured`
         SHANT `abandon property to the Insurer`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC5: the Insured may in no case abandon property to the Insurer")

§§ `GC6, GC8, GC12 and proof of value: duties with no time stated`

@ref GC6, src:892-896
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC6: once the Insurer elects to reinstate, the Insured supplies plans and particulars` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MUST  `supply plans, specifications, quantities and particulars`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC6: plans, specifications and particulars required for reinstatement were not supplied"

@ref GC8, src:916-926
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC8: the claimant does what subrogation requires` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MUST  `do what is required to enforce subrogation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC8: the claimant did not do what the Insurer reasonably required to enforce subrogation"

@ref GC12, src:963-971
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC12: the Insured takes reasonable precautions` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MUST  `take reasonable precautions`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "GC12: reasonable precautions were not taken"

-- Part 1, "Proof of value": the Insured must keep purchase receipts or proof of value of all
-- property insured under Part 1, to prove the value of any loss claimed.
-- src:338 | BẰNG CHỨNG GIÁ TRỊ
-- src:339 | Người Được Bảo Hiểm có nghĩa vụ giữ lại các biên lai mua hàng hoặc bằng chứng về giá trị của tất cả các tài
-- src:340 | sản được bảo hiểm theo quy định trong Phần này để có thể chứng minh giá trị của bất kỳ tổn thất nào nếu
-- src:341 | Người Được Bảo Hiểm yêu cầu bồi thường dưới Phần này.
@ref Part 1, Bằng Chứng Giá Trị, src:338-341
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`Part 1: the Insured keeps proof of value` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MUST  `keep purchase receipts or proof of value`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Insured` BECAUSE "Part 1, proof of value: no receipts or proof of value were kept"

§§ `GC10 and GC11: powers of either party`

@ref GC10, src:939-946
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC10: either party may refer a dispute to VIAC` MEANS
        (PARTY `the Insured` MAY `submit the dispute to VIAC`)
    ROR (PARTY `the Insurer` MAY `submit the dispute to VIAC`)

-- The Insurer's cancellation: a power, and once exercised a duty to refund. No time for the
-- refund is stated, so it carries no WITHIN.
@ref GC11, src:947-952
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC11: the Insurer may cancel, and must then refund` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insurer`
    MAY   `send written notice of cancellation by registered post`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Insurer`
           MUST  `refund premium`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  BREACH BY `the Insurer` BECAUSE "GC11: the unearned premium was not refunded after the Insurer cancelled")

@ref GC11, src:953-956
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the policy`
`GC11: the Insured may cancel at any time, and the Insurer must then refund` MEANS
    PARTY `the Insured`
    MAY   `send written notice of cancellation`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Insurer`
           MUST  `refund premium`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  BREACH BY `the Insurer` BECAUSE "GC11: the short-period refund was not made after the Insured cancelled")
